WEBVTT

00:07.460 --> 00:10.430
Fall in love, boys and girls

00:11.030 --> 00:14.000
Twinkle! Put a star in your eye

00:14.600 --> 00:17.460
The passion, the way it was born

00:17.970 --> 00:20.940
Makes sparks in the jungle! Haré+Guu!

00:21.840 --> 00:24.810
How the hips shake, mucho dizzying

00:25.340 --> 00:28.400
Amigo, that's risky for a kid

00:29.010 --> 00:32.070
If I were to kiss, I'd get sucked in

00:32.650 --> 00:35.050
Tonight, I want to see something scary

00:36.150 --> 00:38.020
Don't be afraid

00:38.020 --> 00:39.860
Going from one push after another

00:39.860 --> 00:41.690
The surprising feeling is nice

00:41.690 --> 00:43.220
And you end up dancing till morning

00:43.790 --> 00:45.230
LOVE LOVE LOVE

00:45.230 --> 00:48.600
TROPICANA

00:50.430 --> 00:53.660
Catch me in the shade under the palm tree

00:54.300 --> 00:57.400
Make me wait, more than down to the limit

00:57.940 --> 01:00.970
I'm sorry, but you're already addicted

01:01.540 --> 01:04.570
From the jungle you can't escape! Haré+Guu!

01:05.280 --> 01:08.220
Fall in love, boys and girls

01:08.790 --> 01:11.780
Twinkle! Put a star in your eye

01:12.360 --> 01:15.420
The passion, the way it was born

01:16.060 --> 01:17.960
Makes sparks in the jungle! Haré+Guu!

01:49.340 --> 01:51.870
What is this... a robot?

01:51.870 --> 01:55.270
He is your partner that will
share the rest of your life with you.

01:55.410 --> 01:56.850
I don't get it!

01:56.850 --> 01:58.750
Why me!?

02:00.480 --> 02:02.040
Let's be friends.

02:13.260 --> 02:14.250
It's them.

02:14.730 --> 02:15.960
What will you do?

02:16.400 --> 02:18.470
Fight with him?

02:18.470 --> 02:19.430
Or...

02:21.040 --> 02:25.730
Dammit, I'll go for it!

02:32.950 --> 02:34.710
Wow!

02:34.880 --> 02:37.220
His character designs are great as always...

02:37.220 --> 02:38.690
The animation staff is pretty great, too.

02:38.690 --> 02:40.180
I'm looking forward to what
happens from here on!

02:41.690 --> 02:44.560
Mo... er, the people in my house,
won't let me watch.

02:44.560 --> 02:45.590
Is it amusing?

02:45.590 --> 02:48.120
Yeah! It's totally okay as a first episode!

02:48.730 --> 02:49.890
You otaku.

02:49.960 --> 02:50.900
Well excuse me!

02:52.470 --> 02:54.200
Oh, I should be getting home soon.

02:54.470 --> 02:55.530
I see...

02:57.310 --> 02:59.070
Please give my regards to your family.

02:59.070 --> 02:59.800
Okay.

02:59.910 --> 03:02.310
So... can I come by again?

03:02.310 --> 03:04.680
Oh, it's not that I'm asking just for the TV.

03:05.050 --> 03:07.640
Of course, Haré-kun, Guu-chan.

03:12.920 --> 03:14.250
Hey, Guu...

03:15.260 --> 03:17.490
Can you go back to the house ahead of me?

03:19.330 --> 03:22.520
I just want to talk with
Grandma a little bit more.

03:22.700 --> 03:23.570
Oh...

03:23.570 --> 03:25.600
So you have yet to reveal your true identity...

03:25.600 --> 03:29.230
...yet you see her repeatedly only for your
own gratification... like parent, like child.

03:29.400 --> 03:31.610
What's that about? You say it in a way that
could cause a misunderstanding!

03:31.610 --> 03:32.270
Am I wrong?

03:32.270 --> 03:33.170
You're wrong!

03:34.940 --> 03:37.040
Fine, you just don't want me to go,
so I won't go!

03:39.150 --> 03:40.380
Stubborn.

03:40.520 --> 03:41.610
I don't want to hear that from you.

03:42.550 --> 03:46.580
You know... wouldn't you feel embarrassed
about revealing your identity at this point?

03:46.920 --> 03:48.580
I missed a good opportunity to tell her.

03:48.720 --> 03:52.690
Nothing like a tsukkomi that misses the
chance to deliver a punch line.

03:52.690 --> 03:55.220
It's not a manzai routine -
wait, I'm the tsukkomi!?

03:55.330 --> 03:57.230
So Guu is the boke?

03:57.230 --> 03:58.170
So shocking!

03:58.170 --> 03:59.130
Cut it out!
So shocking!

04:00.740 --> 04:03.830
I do want Mom and Grandma to make up...

04:04.140 --> 04:06.370
But I don't want to force it.

04:06.370 --> 04:08.540
I want the two of them to
patch things up on their own.

04:08.940 --> 04:12.440
Mom's at the heart of this, but I don't know
how she feels at all...

04:13.510 --> 04:15.280
Hey! What are you doing, Guu?

04:17.950 --> 04:20.010
I'm talking about something important here!

04:22.960 --> 04:23.890
Hey, Mom?

04:24.960 --> 04:27.430
I know it's weird for me to ask...

04:28.200 --> 04:29.660
...but why did we come back here?

04:30.330 --> 04:31.330
Why?

04:31.330 --> 04:33.030
Because I wanted to come back.

04:33.230 --> 04:34.930
You know...

04:35.000 --> 04:37.600
What? You want to go back now, too?

04:38.270 --> 04:39.400
To the jungle.

04:39.640 --> 04:43.600
Over... It's All Over

04:47.580 --> 04:49.240
The jungle, huh...

04:50.650 --> 04:52.520
I wonder how everyone is doing.

04:57.530 --> 04:59.120
The memories are coming back...

05:02.300 --> 05:04.460
What the hell is that cheap prop for!?

05:05.100 --> 05:08.370
Please, stop playing with my feelings.

05:08.370 --> 05:11.100
Even without you doing this,
I have so many things on my mind.

05:11.270 --> 05:12.800
Oh, like what?

05:12.870 --> 05:17.010
Like, what did Mom mean by all of this, or
how long we're going to stay here...

05:17.010 --> 05:19.750
...or how are Marie and Ravenna and Laya
and the others are doing...

05:19.750 --> 05:23.840
I want to know, and it would be nice if I could
drop by there and hurry back here...

05:25.950 --> 05:28.510
Then, I will rid you of your worries.

05:29.420 --> 05:31.320
What, the Chinchikurin Stick again?

05:31.460 --> 05:32.090
No.

05:32.090 --> 05:35.860
To gain more viewers for the show, we're
introducing a new item.

05:35.860 --> 05:37.460
See, you're an otaku, too.

05:37.700 --> 05:40.870
It only takes an instant if you ride a robot.

05:40.870 --> 05:41.970
That's impossible.

05:41.970 --> 05:43.500
In the first place, where is there a robot
around here?

05:43.500 --> 05:45.400
Well, wait a minute, I'll prepare it now.

05:45.470 --> 05:46.460
Prepare it?

05:47.240 --> 05:49.510
Eh? Is this the cockpit?

05:49.510 --> 05:51.310
What should we do, Seiichi-kun?

05:51.310 --> 05:52.940
Let's hurry up and clean up this place.

05:53.010 --> 05:54.080
You know, it's pretty cluttered.

05:54.080 --> 05:54.880
We need to hurry.

06:41.130 --> 06:42.490
Yoohoo, Haré-Haré.

06:42.630 --> 06:44.190
Thanks for what you did the other day.

06:44.400 --> 06:47.600
These two... How did they clean up this
place, and how did they get this all ready?

06:48.870 --> 06:51.360
What's wrong? Pilot this thing to your
heart's content!

06:51.440 --> 06:52.240
Shut up!

06:52.240 --> 06:55.970
Well now, Haré-kun, we cleaned up just for
this, so let's have a good time with it, okay?

06:56.110 --> 06:58.310
That's right. You've got the
wrong groove for this, Haré-Haré.

06:58.810 --> 07:03.010
I hate coming here because I always feel like
I'm the odd one.

07:03.120 --> 07:03.910
C-Come to think of it...

07:04.420 --> 07:05.480
Where's Yamada-san?

07:06.320 --> 07:07.290
You called?

07:07.490 --> 07:08.820
She's totally blended in!

07:08.890 --> 07:10.260
And there's no tension here at all!

07:10.460 --> 07:13.480
I-It looks like you've gotten used to living
here, Yamada-san.

07:13.960 --> 07:14.960
Well, yeah.

07:14.960 --> 07:17.100
When you get the hang of it, it's a breeze.

07:17.100 --> 07:17.930
The hang of it?

07:17.930 --> 07:20.700
It's best to not think about
anything when you're here.

07:20.870 --> 07:23.700
Can you actually say that you're living as a
human when you do that?

07:24.270 --> 07:26.740
When you get used to it,
living like this is easy.

07:28.580 --> 07:29.800
A useless person.

07:31.410 --> 07:33.140
Not good... if I stay here for too long,
it's dangerous.

07:33.210 --> 07:35.850
I'll hurry up and play around for a little while
so Guu feels satisfied, and get the heck out.

07:35.850 --> 07:36.680
A-All right...

07:36.880 --> 07:38.580
Which one is the main lever?

07:44.560 --> 07:45.360
Oh well.

07:45.790 --> 07:47.520
Anyway, let's go!

07:53.130 --> 07:56.300
Somehow, it really feel like
I'm operating a robot!

07:59.540 --> 08:01.370
Oh, Guu-sama, are you stepping out?

08:02.110 --> 08:03.780
No it doesn't!

08:03.780 --> 08:04.570
What's wrong?

08:04.810 --> 08:09.770
Well, it's lacking oomph.
It would feel more like it if there was some
grand action or something...

08:10.080 --> 08:13.080
But more than that, it's impossible to get to
the jungle at this slow speed.

08:13.490 --> 08:15.390
Then push the B button.

08:15.520 --> 08:16.620
The B button?

08:16.960 --> 08:17.550
This one?

08:20.130 --> 08:21.990
What...!? What's going on!?

08:22.500 --> 08:24.930
Look beside you, at the mirror to your side.

08:27.540 --> 08:29.000
Let me down!

08:30.240 --> 08:31.640
...I've had enough.

08:31.640 --> 08:32.970
Now, don't say that.

08:33.270 --> 08:34.940
Oh, but what does the A button do?

08:34.940 --> 08:37.140
The romanticism of robots will take shape!

08:37.480 --> 08:38.910
A rocket punch or something?

08:38.980 --> 08:40.500
The romanticism of robots.

08:40.820 --> 08:42.370
That is, self-destruction!

08:44.090 --> 08:45.920
Time left until detonation:

08:45.920 --> 08:48.820
Stop it!
6... 5... 4... 3... 2... 1...

08:52.260 --> 08:54.090
I-I've been spared...

08:54.160 --> 08:57.600
What's with you!? I wanted you
to feel the romanticism!

08:58.530 --> 09:00.300
Don't be cute about snapping at me!

09:00.300 --> 09:01.240
Meow!

09:01.240 --> 09:02.290
That's enough.

09:02.500 --> 09:04.490
I've had enough with the robot.

09:04.640 --> 09:07.200
I won't say that I want to go back to the
jungle ever again.

09:07.480 --> 09:09.600
You're fine with not being able to see them
ever again?

09:11.480 --> 09:13.140
I don't want that...

09:13.310 --> 09:16.610
Not being able to see them again? That's...

09:17.620 --> 09:20.350
I mean, in either case,
I can't stay in either place.

09:20.350 --> 09:23.790
I do want to go back to the jungle, but there
are reasons for me to stay here also...

09:24.590 --> 09:27.220
Geez, you really cause
me so much trouble, meow!

09:27.600 --> 09:30.090
All right, I have no choice
but to rewrite the program.

09:30.160 --> 09:32.000
Wait, what random thing are you...

09:36.300 --> 09:38.610
Wow! It's the school!
It brings back memories!

09:38.610 --> 09:40.700
Sorry to borrow it for so long,

09:41.440 --> 09:42.430
You're done with it now?

09:42.540 --> 09:44.450
Yeah, I already bought the other book,
Now, hurry up and control it.

09:44.450 --> 09:45.080
Yeah, I already bought the other book,
What's this controller?

09:45.080 --> 09:46.380
This is a great book, isn't it?
What's this controller?

09:46.380 --> 09:48.110
It's the remote-control for Gupta!

09:48.650 --> 09:51.780
You know, stop with those kind of jokes!

09:51.850 --> 09:55.020
You can have a conversation
through the mic on the controller.

09:55.020 --> 09:55.720
Mic?

09:56.320 --> 09:57.190
Oh, you're right.

09:57.590 --> 09:59.890
But to suddenly have a conversation...

10:00.290 --> 10:01.990
Hey, hello, Gupta?

10:02.100 --> 10:02.820
How are you doing?

10:04.370 --> 10:05.350
What's wrong?

10:05.600 --> 10:07.500
Something like a mosquito...

10:07.670 --> 10:08.730
Useless!

10:09.000 --> 10:12.600
Now, now, control him just like Guu
commands.

10:13.210 --> 10:14.570
Now, move forward.

10:14.680 --> 10:16.010
Oh, sure, right, right.

10:17.140 --> 10:18.270
Now, stop.

10:19.610 --> 10:20.640
Now, move back.

10:22.180 --> 10:23.080
Stop.

10:23.780 --> 10:24.810
I found a coin.

10:24.920 --> 10:26.180
Oh, you're right.

10:26.390 --> 10:27.510
That seemed natural, didn't it?

10:27.620 --> 10:29.280
It was so natural that
I couldn't see anything unusual!

10:29.360 --> 10:33.190
Listen up, okay? The amazing thing about
this game is in the hidden commands.

10:33.190 --> 10:34.720
This isn't a game.

10:34.860 --> 10:38.490
Just push A, A, B, A, B.
Something good will happen.

10:38.830 --> 10:39.800
That better be true.

10:39.870 --> 10:40.700
Sure, sure!

10:44.470 --> 10:45.060
See?

10:45.240 --> 10:46.510
I don't care about that!

10:46.510 --> 10:48.440
Now, let's try Lazy next.

10:48.440 --> 10:50.270
Everything is okay just by you saying
"Let's do it"!?

10:50.540 --> 10:52.940
This is too arbitrary! It's unsettling!

10:54.050 --> 10:56.880
Geez, Big Brother, you need to wake up for
your meal, at the least!

10:57.990 --> 10:59.480
I'm up, I'm up...

10:59.550 --> 11:00.420
Geez...

11:00.860 --> 11:02.460
As always, he's asleep...

11:02.460 --> 11:04.360
Oh, but if I pushed this switch,
he might wake up.

11:08.630 --> 11:09.730
What's wrong?

11:09.730 --> 11:11.930
Is something on my face or something?

11:12.770 --> 11:15.670
Something good needs to happen!
Something, anything!

11:15.740 --> 11:17.100
It's not all that good...

11:17.100 --> 11:18.470
Don't you say that!

11:18.470 --> 11:21.780
After all, it's not that much fun unless it's
someone close to you!

11:21.780 --> 11:24.580
It's not a problem of
whether or not this is fun!

11:24.580 --> 11:26.380
We need to use this person.

11:26.380 --> 11:27.240
Who?

11:30.920 --> 11:31.890
Letters?

11:32.090 --> 11:33.990
Let's control Weda!

11:34.090 --> 11:36.450
S-S-S-Stop it! I've had enough of...

11:42.100 --> 11:44.330
What did you do? What did you do? What did
you do? What did you do? What did...

11:45.530 --> 11:48.000
We're going back to the jungle.

11:49.370 --> 11:51.360
We're going back to the jungle.

11:52.070 --> 11:53.560
The story so far:

11:53.640 --> 11:56.410
Haré is a clumsy, foolish,
perverted young boy.

11:56.410 --> 12:00.180
In front of him appears Guu, a lovely and
pretty girl, and for some reason they start to
live together.

12:00.180 --> 12:02.840
It's the beginning of a lovey-dovey,
heart-racing life!

12:03.880 --> 12:05.180
That's completely wrong!

12:05.250 --> 12:07.990
What's wrong? You wanted
to go back home so much...

12:07.990 --> 12:11.010
That's true, but there are parts
of me that don't want to...

12:11.260 --> 12:12.250
Which is it?

12:12.360 --> 12:14.160
Well, um, if I had to decide...

12:14.160 --> 12:14.700
Then, we're going back.
Well, um, if I had to decide...

12:14.700 --> 12:15.160
Then, we're going back.

12:15.160 --> 12:15.860
It's been decided now!

12:15.860 --> 12:17.130
I haven't said anything!

12:17.430 --> 12:20.090
Kids listen to what their parents have to say.

12:20.400 --> 12:21.330
O-Okay...

12:22.800 --> 12:23.940
W-Why?

12:23.940 --> 12:24.670
That's right!

12:24.670 --> 12:26.140
If I use Guu's controller once more...

12:26.210 --> 12:26.730
Here.

12:27.340 --> 12:28.400
All right...

12:34.220 --> 12:34.940
Haré!

12:36.120 --> 12:36.950
Mom!

12:37.520 --> 12:39.490
I reserved the tickets. Flight's tonight.

12:39.550 --> 12:40.920
The situation got worse!

12:40.990 --> 12:42.960
M-Mom, seriously, hold on a second here.

12:42.960 --> 12:44.460
This is all because of Guu's controller.

12:44.460 --> 12:46.790
It's not that you really want
to go back to the jungle, Mom...

12:46.790 --> 12:47.920
Ojou-sama!

12:48.200 --> 12:49.660
Ojou-sama, say it isn't so!

12:49.660 --> 12:51.100
Please tell me that it's all a lie!

12:51.170 --> 12:53.430
Say it's a lie, a bad dream, a little
mischievous prank you pulled!

12:53.500 --> 12:55.440
It's been 11 years
since you left this house, Ojou-sama!

12:55.440 --> 12:57.200
It's been 11 years for me!

12:57.200 --> 13:00.410
How many times I've dreamt of
bowing down to you in this mansion,
to serve you, Ojou-sama!

13:00.410 --> 13:04.470
And now! Finally!! I am able to be at your
side like this, Ojou-sama!

13:04.550 --> 13:06.540
Ojou-san, will one suitcase be enough?

13:08.220 --> 13:12.240
D-D-D-D-Did I do
something that displeased you?

13:12.350 --> 13:13.920
More than enough things.

13:13.920 --> 13:15.080
I've already decided!

13:15.960 --> 13:17.060
Impossible! Impossible! Impossible...

13:17.060 --> 13:18.430
H-H-H-Hold on a second, Mom.

13:18.430 --> 13:19.450
What is it?

13:19.530 --> 13:22.430
Well, this isn't something
to chat about while standing.

13:22.430 --> 13:24.760
Actually, we're already sitting, but all that
aside, how about some tea?

13:25.100 --> 13:26.730
That was really forced.

13:26.930 --> 13:28.400
I'm desperate, you know.

13:29.600 --> 13:33.730
Ojou-sama, you like milk in your tea, right?

13:33.970 --> 13:37.110
I'd like her to cry or make tea,
but not both at the same time.

13:37.110 --> 13:38.410
I-I know!

13:38.480 --> 13:42.280
I'm not sure if you know about this,
Ojou-sama, but we're building a fountain in
the west annex!

13:42.280 --> 13:45.810
When it's done, it will be running a fountain
of alcohol, not water!

13:45.950 --> 13:47.890
You know, that's such a terrible lie that not
even kids would fall for it.

13:47.890 --> 13:48.750
How wonderful!

13:48.920 --> 13:49.860
And she's taking it seriously!!

13:49.860 --> 13:52.060
That's not all.
Every faucet will be running alcohol!

13:52.060 --> 13:54.080
Even the bath will be all alcohol!

13:54.660 --> 13:56.430
I can't get enough of that!

13:56.430 --> 13:57.290
But, I don't want it after all.

13:57.360 --> 13:58.060
Why!?

13:58.270 --> 14:01.600
Things that flaunt money like
that are like my father. I don't like it.

14:02.470 --> 14:05.470
Senpai, it's impossible. Our ojou-san is a
tremendously stubborn person.

14:05.470 --> 14:06.840
It's useless to try to hold her back.

14:07.440 --> 14:10.640
What's with this "Tremendously stubborn,"
and how it's useless to hold her back!?

14:10.640 --> 14:13.700
I'm the only one that can
talk that way about Ojou-sama!

14:14.010 --> 14:15.920
In any case, we're definitely going back!

14:15.920 --> 14:18.110
Haré, gather your belongings and go change.

14:18.190 --> 14:19.710
Ojou-sama!

14:35.300 --> 14:36.630
Mother...

14:43.440 --> 14:45.680
What? You still haven't changed?

14:45.680 --> 14:46.810
Hurry up.

14:47.280 --> 14:48.040
Yeah...

14:54.690 --> 14:55.280
Guu.

14:56.020 --> 14:57.890
I'm going to go see Grandma.

14:58.430 --> 15:01.790
I have a feeling that if I don't see her now, I'll
definitely regret it later.

15:03.000 --> 15:04.160
Go ahead and go.

15:04.230 --> 15:05.030
Thanks.

15:34.060 --> 15:35.790
What's wrong, Haré-kun?

15:39.270 --> 15:42.900
When we first me,
you talked about your kids, right?

15:42.970 --> 15:45.400
Y-Yes.

15:46.140 --> 15:47.800
Do you still want to see your child?

15:48.240 --> 15:50.470
Yes, of course.

15:51.080 --> 15:55.210
Then, if you want to see her, I think you have
to be the one to go out and see her.

15:56.720 --> 15:59.740
She's somewhere near you, right?
Then, it will take only a moment!

15:59.850 --> 16:03.050
Me, when I feel that I want to see someone,
I go out myself to see that person!

16:04.330 --> 16:07.890
Because if I rely on someone else,
the result isn't meaningful!

16:12.300 --> 16:14.600
Did I say something that I shouldn't have?

16:16.400 --> 16:17.500
Maybe I did.

16:18.540 --> 16:19.400
U-Um...

16:23.710 --> 16:25.810
Ah! I-I'm sorry!

16:25.810 --> 16:27.150
I'm sorry, I said something
that I shouldn't have!

16:27.150 --> 16:29.910
But, somehow, I felt like
I really needed to say it...

16:30.850 --> 16:32.050
No...

16:32.050 --> 16:35.580
I'm sorry! There are all sorts of reasons why
you wouldn't be able to see her...

16:39.560 --> 16:43.160
I'm really sorry... for making you feel bad...

16:52.640 --> 16:54.070
11 years...

16:55.680 --> 16:57.540
For 11 years, I...

16:58.550 --> 17:03.240
I hadn't been able to move at all from that
day when she left this house...

17:06.420 --> 17:10.750
Why wasn't I able to
embrace her on that day?

17:11.460 --> 17:17.160
That no matter who she was, no matter what
she did, I would love her regardless...

17:17.870 --> 17:19.770
Why wasn't I able to tell her that?

17:38.620 --> 17:39.550
I guess...

17:39.550 --> 17:41.210
...it's no good at this point...

17:42.120 --> 17:43.220
It was too late after all.

17:43.220 --> 17:44.560
Oh brother...

17:44.560 --> 17:48.120
This is why humans always miss good
opportunities...

17:51.170 --> 17:52.150
That's true.

17:52.700 --> 17:55.130
I always do things at the wrong time.

18:01.980 --> 18:03.170
Haré!

18:03.340 --> 18:04.650
Hurry!

18:04.650 --> 18:06.610
We'll be late for our flight!

18:06.680 --> 18:07.410
Mom!

18:07.410 --> 18:07.970
What?

18:08.920 --> 18:10.440
Well, um...

18:11.690 --> 18:15.310
If I were, for some reason, no longer be able
to live in the jungle village...

18:15.860 --> 18:18.650
What would you do?

18:20.460 --> 18:21.450
Why do you ask?

18:22.100 --> 18:22.930
Well...

18:23.000 --> 18:28.800
S-So, the other day, I met this person whose
child left for somewhere else, just like that.

18:29.770 --> 18:32.240
I wouldn't leave you alone.

18:34.210 --> 18:39.650
I wouldn't make my child feel that way.

19:11.780 --> 19:12.840
That's right.

19:13.110 --> 19:17.350
I already have a child, and know how a
mother feels...

19:19.520 --> 19:22.280
I would never leave this child alone.

19:22.690 --> 19:25.180
No matter how much she
writes letters to me and says that she wants
to see me, I won't believe it.

19:25.990 --> 19:28.430
I'd leave the village with you.

19:30.130 --> 19:32.290
Would things work out that easily?

19:33.100 --> 19:37.570
There are always people who have fatally
bad timing for everything.

19:37.570 --> 19:38.540
T-That's right!

19:38.540 --> 19:41.410
What would you do if you missed your
chance, and you didn't make it in time?

19:41.410 --> 19:46.000
If you didn't make it in time, and I had to be
separated from you, Mom...

19:46.480 --> 19:47.670
...if you couldn't see me anymore,
what would you do?

19:52.090 --> 19:53.280
I get it...

19:58.030 --> 20:03.620
I have a child now,
and know how a mother feels...

20:04.400 --> 20:13.430
...so it's easy for me to imagine
how hard it is, how sad it is, for your child to
vanish from sight...

20:18.780 --> 20:22.910
Every day I'm sure that I'd think about how I
want to see you.

20:23.020 --> 20:26.320
I would, too! I'd think about how
I want to see you, Mom!

20:26.950 --> 20:31.820
Why didn't I even try to understand how hard
it was on my mother that day as well?

20:36.700 --> 20:38.860
I want to see her too, my mother...

20:39.730 --> 20:44.360
Besides, I have to give her
a proper introduction to my son,
someone I can be proud of.

21:12.730 --> 21:15.630
Now then, you've got something
that needs said here, right?

21:18.910 --> 21:20.200
Welcome back...

21:24.110 --> 21:25.100
I'm home.
